    // For python, missing gives generic, not friendly. So if None, attempt spawn with "python3" to get generic error? Original with empty PATH (no python3/python) gave generic "No such file...". How to replicate? Attempt ProcCommand::new("python3") which will fail with NotFound, then print generic.
    if bin.is_none() {
        // Attempt spawn to get generic error? Or directly print generic?
        // Original runs dotnet --list-sdks (ignored), then tries python3 --version? Or directly python3 -c? With missing, version check would fail (no binary), but version failure for python is ignored? Actually for python missing, it gave generic, not friendly. That suggests it doesn't give friendly for version missing, just tries execution and fails generic.
        // So we should attempt execution with "python3" (unresolved) and let it fail.
        let mut cmd = ProcCommand::new("python3");
